## integration commits beyond the merges

=================== 547d65d
547d65d Integration (round 2): compile reconciliation WS-6 x WS-7 in memory::profile

WS-7 (P2-AR-0028) removed capabilities::governance::command_files (its TOFU
pin helper); WS-6 (P2-AR-0027) imports it for the retrieval-profile adapter
identity. The listing WS-6 was built and tested against is kept as a private
helper in memory/profile.rs with identical behaviour. WS-7's execution binding
(capabilities::binding::resolve) is untouched and still decides which bytes a
plugin may run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>


 runtime/src/memory/profile.rs | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

=================== bcf0139
bcf0139 Integration (round 2): WS-4 x WS-5 — propagation re-seals the OS-sealed records it marks stale

WS-5 (P2-AR-0026) T2-seals close reports at task close and establishes recorded
authorship (BC-P2-34) and close attribution only from reports whose seal
verifies. WS-4 (P2-AR-0025, BC-P2-04) marks the closing reports of dependent
work stale during CIT-E propagation. In the union the staleness marker broke the
report's seal, so the report stopped counting as recorded authorship
(greenfield_end_to_end: INDEPENDENCE_VIOLATION on TST-0001) and would be
reported as T2 tampering by WS-2's os_binding_integrity.

cit::propagation::save_set (the single writer of propagation markers) now
re-seals a record after marking it only when its seal verified before the write
(operation "cit propagation"); a record whose seal does not verify is marked but
never sealed, so the OS never blesses content it did not write (the rule WS-10's
lifecycle::record_influence already applies). This is the first option WS-5
stated for its IP-R3-3. No check is relaxed: a hand edit of a report still
breaks its seal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>


 runtime/src/cit/propagation.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

=================== 9c4af7e
9c4af7e Integration (round 2): converge the certification harness on WS-8's provisioned root; builder-test updates

One harness convention (P2-HO-0030; WS-3 IP-R2-4; WS-8 IP-R2-WS08-12): every
scenario machine is provisioned with the suite's throw-away root (which
delegates human-gate to the test owner) and installs releases signed under it.
No assertion is removed or weakened; every change is listed with its reason.

Harness convergence
- ws03.rs: throwaway_root/provision/signed_release/break_glass_for and the
  re-anchor publisher now delegate to common::{suite_root_file, provision
  (idempotent), sign_release, break_glass} — one root for the whole suite
  (identical key material and human-gate delegation). The P2-ADJ-0001 test is
  about an unprovisioned machine, so it uses WS-8's fresh_unprovisioned.
- ws04r2.rs, ws05.rs, ws06.rs, ws07.rs: `init --source signed_source()` on the
  provisioned scenario machine (the embedded payload without signed metadata is
  refused SRR_RELEASE_UNVERIFIED on a provisioned machine, R1 behaviour).
- ws08_r2.rs newer_external: the hypothetical 9.9.9 release keeps only its own
  step from the current version; the canonical tree now also carries WS-9's
  prepared M-4.1.5-4.1.6, and the chain resolver follows the first step.

Builder tests meeting other workstreams' round-2 rules
- ws03 round-two call sites: WS-9 (P2-AR-0030) resolves the adoption actor
  against the process declaration and records its channel
  ("session: flag; role: flag") instead of the literal "declared".
- ws06: WS-7 BC-P2-39 — the local embedder and the rerank plugin are registered
  through ws07::register_approved; the revision-2 descriptor is first shown not
  to execute unregistered, then registered, so WS-6's revision-pin refusal is
  what is measured. WS-5 BC-P2-16 — the implementation task declares its
  scenario and acceptance test (ws05::traceable_inputs) so it is claimable.
- ws04r2 upstream change: WS-5 BC-P2-20 — the close report is a consumption
  receipt (ws05::receipt); with WS-2's close gate (BC-P2-43) the fixture, which
  runs no product tests, states not_applicable_with_reason.
- ws08_r2 adopt ingress: WS-9 BC-P2-34 — the designated reviewer authors tests
  before approving (migration::reviewer_authors_tests).
- repair::task_close_enforces_mutation_scope: the governed CIT executes before
  the out-of-scope write instead of while it is on disk (see the integration
  report: WS-2 W7 remediation x WS-4 G4-after-CIT-E x WS-5 close gate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>


